From 8f8d30a91aafaaf027d93e0ae97b348fa220d333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: C0fuge <189659128+C0fuge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:49:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libhdfs3: AES/CTR cipher option for data-transfer privacy
 (dfs.encrypt.data.transfer.cipher.suites)

With dfs.data.transfer.protection=privacy and dfs.encrypt.data.transfer.cipher.suites=AES/CTR/NoPadding
the client offers an AES/CTR CipherOptionProto with its DIGEST-MD5 response (as SaslDataTransferClient).
If the DataNode accepts it, its keys are unwrapped with the auth-conf session and the connection
continues as a plain AES-CTR stream (AesCtrSocket) instead of DIGEST-MD5 3des frames.
---
